2026-07 [Ghidra, session 3] RECLASSIFIED AGAIN, superseding the 2025 entry above: all 10 tables in the f3a8/f3aa/f3ac/f3ae/f3b0/f3b2 cluster (the 4 "TCU Torque Ramp Target" tables + the 6 "Open Loop Lambda ..." tables) are confirmed to be a single SHARED "Knock-to-TCU Torque Coordination" register group, category changed to Knock Control. Confirmed via matching enable-condition disassembly in both tcu_rx_main_scheduler and knock_process_main (identical RAM 0xf1f2 bit7 gate). This was checked specifically to rule out address aliasing/misidentification - see logging.txt session 3 "0xF3AC/0xF3AE CONFLICT - CONFIRMED INTENTIONAL" for the full resolution. Table names updated in place; old "Lambda ..." names kept parenthetically for continuity with prior tuning notes. Treat the AFR/uint8 scaling on the ex-Lambda tables as SUSPECT pending further work - the dual TCU/knock interpretation of the same bytes is confirmed, but which (if either) numeric scaling is correct is not yet resolved.
2026-07 [Ghidra, session 4] Octane Level (MUT 0x27, RAM 0xEEC8/EEC9) decay-vs-knock mechanism confirmed and documented in RVR_base.xml's shared notes section - this is the "knock retard" equivalent on this ECU (no discrete retard-degrees value exists). See RVR_base.xml notes and logging.txt session 4 for full detail.
